"><span>(d)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Length of <strong><em>building</em></strong> wall <br><br>The maximum length of any <strong><em>story</em></strong> located above a height of 500 feet shall not exceed 250 feet. Such length shall be measured by inscribing within a rectangle the outermost walls at the level of each <strong><em>story</em></strong> entirely above a height of 500 feet. No side of such rectangle shall exceed a width of 250 feet. </span></p>","plainText":"(d) Length of building wall The maximum length of any story located above a height of 500 feet shall not exceed 250 feet. Such length shall be measured by inscribing within a rectangle the outermost walls at the level of each story entirely above a height of 500 feet. No side of such rectangle shall exceed a width of 250 feet."},{"id":"zr-19504-block-027","kind":"html","html":"<p style=\"margin-left: 43pt;text-indent: -43pt;\"><span></span></p>","plainText":""},{"id":"zr-19504-block-028","kind":"html","html":"<p style=\"margin-left: 43pt;text-indent: -43pt;\"><span></span></p>","plainText":""},{"id":"zr-19504-block-029","kind":"html","html":"<p style=\"margin-left: 43pt;text-indent: -43pt;\"><span></span></p>","plainText":""}],"zoning":{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceNodeID":19504,"sourcePath":"/article-ix/chapter-3/93-42","sourceURL":"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ix/chapter-3/93-42","sourceContentHash":"10a7c45939f28595834b8ac829136a4a115ff14c092f5246c205eb055288db2c","article":{"roman":"IX","title":"Special Purpose Districts"},"chapter":{"number":"3","title":"Special Hudson Yards District (HY)","canonicalNumber":"IX-3"},"appendix":null,"subsections":[{"id":"zr-19504-sub-b63a2383c1bcc004","label":"(a)","sourceAnchor":null,"plainText":"(a) Maximum base heightsThe maximum height of a building or other structure before setback shall be 150 feet along a wide street and along a narrow street within 100 feet of its intersection with a wide street, and 90 feet along a narrow street beyond 100 feet of its intersection with a wide street. For corner lots with wide street frontage and more than 100 feet of narrow street frontage, the maximum building height before setback along the narrow street may, as an alternative, be the weighted average of 150 feet for the first 100 feet from the corner, and 90 feet for the remainder of the narrow street frontage. Such allowable maximum heights before required setbacks are hereinafter referred to as “maximum base heights.”","ordinal":0},{"id":"zr-19504-sub-24ecc50aaef169fe","label":"(b)","sourceAnchor":null,"plainText":"(b) Required setbacksFor buildings that contain only residential use above the applicable maximum base height, the required minimum setback for portions of such buildings that exceed such maximum base height shall be 10 feet from a wide street and 15 feet from a narrow street.For buildings or other structures that contain commercial or community facility use above the applicable maximum base height, the required minimum setback for portions of buildings or other structures that exceed such maximum base height shall be 15 feet from a wide street and 20 feet from a narrow street.","ordinal":1},{"id":"zr-19504-sub-b6c928ec9ed387cc","label":"(c)","sourceAnchor":null,"plainText":"(c) Tower lot coverage The portion of any building or buildings located above a height of 150 feet are hereinafter referred to as “towers.”","ordinal":2},{"id":"zr-19504-sub-11af40b76b97d444","label":"(1)","sourceAnchor":null,"plainText":"(1) Towers containing residences shall occupy, in the aggregate, a minimum of 30 percent of the lot area of the zoning lot, except that this requirement shall not apply to the highest 40 feet of such tower or towers. Furthermore, towers containing residences shall occupy not more than 40 percent of the lot area of the zoning lot or, for zoning lots less than 20,000 square feet, the percentage set forth in the following table:","ordinal":3},{"id":"zr-19504-sub-3f29c2be5bdbfbd6","label":"(2)","sourceAnchor":null,"plainText":"(2) Towers that contain only commercial or community facility use, or a combination thereof, shall occupy not more than 60 percent of the lot area of the zoning lot or, for zoning lots less than 30,000 square feet, the percentage set forth in the following table:","ordinal":4},{"id":"zr-19504-sub-faebe2bd9f030765","label":"(d)","sourceAnchor":null,"plainText":"(d) Length of building wall The maximum length of any story located above a height of 500 feet shall not exceed 250 feet. Such length shall be measured by inscribing within a rectangle the outermost walls at the level of each story entirely above a height of 500 feet. No side of such rectangle shall exceed a width of 250 feet.","ordinal":5}],"tables":[{"id":"zr-19504-table-001","ordinal":0,"sourceAnchor":null,"caption":null,"plainText":"Area of Zoning Lot (in square feet)Maximum Percentage of Lot Coverage 10,500 or less5010,501 to 11,5004911,501 to 12,5004812,501 to 13,5004713,501 to 14,5004614,501 to 15,5004515,501 to 16,5004416,501 to 17,5004317,501 to 18,5004218,501 to 19,99941","contentHash":"630c22e44a17f49da3fe0b31ec330998fa42c687ca60ca6305fe292fd75f5937"},{"id":"zr-19504-table-002","ordinal":1,"sourceAnchor":null,"caption":null,"plainText":"Area of Zoning Lot (in square feet)Maximum Percentage of Lot Coverage 20,500 or less7020,501 to 21,5006921,501 to 22,5006822,501 to 23,5006723,501 to 24,5006624,501 to 25,5006525,501 to 26,5006426,501 to 27,5006327,501 to 28,5006228,501 to 29,99961","contentHash":"edc6a71a4e1172ad14bb7be1c1f4c313142217652f48fef42bf65bba306fc64b"}],"mapReferences":[],"appendixReferences":[],"specialDistrict":{"name":"Special Hudson Yards District (HY)","abbreviation":"HY"},"amendmentHistory":[{"effectiveDate":"2011-02-02","reportNumber":"N110090AZRY","reportURL":"http://a030-cpc.nyc.gov/html/cpc/report.aspx?num=N%20110090a%20ZRY","projectName":"KEY TERMS CLARIFICATION TEXT","action":"Amended","notes":"Key Terms","description":"TEXT AMENDMENT TO CLARIFY AND PRESERVE THE INTENT OF THE ZONING REGULATIONS IN RELATION TO THE TERMS \"DEVELOPMENT\" AND \"BUILDING\" AS DEFINED IN THE ZONING RESOLUTION"},{"effectiveDate":"2009-12-21","reportNumber":"N090434ZRM","reportURL":"http://a030-cpc.nyc.gov/html/cpc/report.aspx?num=N%20090434%20ZRM","projectName":"WESTERN RAIL YARD TEXT","action":"Amended","notes":"Western Rail Yard-Subdistrict F","description":"TEXT AMEND TO THE SPECIAL HUDSON YARDS DIST MAKING THE PRO- JECT SITE A NEW SUBAREA WITHIN THE SPECIAL HUDSON YARD DIST"},{"effectiveDate":"2005-12-21","reportNumber":"N060046AZRM","reportURL":"http://a030-cpc.nyc.gov/html/cpc/report.aspx?num=N%20060046a%20ZRM","projectName":"HUDSON YARDS","action":"Amended","notes":"HY FUCA","description":"ADDITIONAL TEXT AMENDMENTS CONSISTS OF 17 CHANGES FROM THE ORIGINAL TEXT & 2 TECHNICAL CLARIFICATIONS"},{"effectiveDate":"2005-01-19","reportNumber":"N040500AZRM","reportURL":"http://a030-cpc.nyc.gov/html/cpc/report.aspx?num=N%20040500a%20ZRM","projectName":"HUDSON YARDS","action":"Added","notes":null,"description":"1ST MOD TO CLARIFY & REVISE CERTAIN SECTIONS OF THE TEXT"}],"amendmentHistorySourceURL":"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/ajax/get/amendment/section/19504","effectiveDate":"2011-02-02","lastAmended":"2011-02-02","version":"NYC Zoning Resolution — text through 2026-07-16","researchEligibility":false}}
